  "raw": {
    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Assistant-Director--Strategic-Communications_R114113": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Strategic Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics   UCF Athletics at the University of Central Florida, an NCAA Division I institution and Big XII Conference member, is seeking applications for the position of Assistant Director, Strategic Communications. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assist in the day-to-day operations of the Strategic Communications department under the direction of the Assistant AD for Strategic Communications. Serve as the primary media contact for women’s basketball, volleyball and other sports programs as assigned. Develop and implement comprehensive communications strategies for assigned sports. Coordinate media relations, travel and gameday communications operations for assigned sports. Promote UCF Athletics through the department’s official website and social media platforms, as well as through relationships with local, regional and national media. Ensure all responsibilities are performed in accordance with UCF, conference and NCAA rules and regulations. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and two (2) years of appropriate experience. Appropriate graduate coursework or master’s degree may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred Qualifications: Communications or sports information experience at the collegiate level or higher. Working knowledge of Adobe InDesign and Photoshop, Microsoft Office Suite and Genius software. Strong communication, organizational, writing, editing and social media skills. ​ Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time and occasional travel. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
    },
    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Director--Sports-Nutrition_R114062-1": {
      "title": "Director, Sports Nutrition",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics   The University of Central Florida, in Orlando, Florida is seeking a Director, Performance Nutrition for UCF Athletics. Under the direction of the Deputy A.D., Athlete Development and Leadership / SWA, the selected candidate will be responsible for the administration, organization, and supervision of a progressive performance nutrition department and oversees meal operations / catering that supports the dietary and hydration needs of 16 NCAA Division I sports and 450+ student-athletes within UCF, Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Research of best practices/protocols in the operation of a full-service training table and multiple fueling stations located on/off campus, as well as oversight of the daily menu/catering available to constituents in terms of quantity and quality of food; Research and collaboration with internal and campus entities in the continuing education and counsel of student-athletes on optimal nutrition and hydration practices to support health and performance; Research and educate / counsel coaches / student-athletes regarding appropriate legal / NCAA compliant use of dietary supplements, herbal supplements, and performance-enhancing substances, to include regular evaluation of NCAA compliant products to be available / consumed by student-athletes, as well as the identification of restricted and banned substances in compliance with governing sport bodies (e.g. NCAA,WADA, US anti-doping agency); Collaboration with coaching staffs and sports performance coaches in the analysis of energy needs / utilization related to each sport and the development of individualized nutrition plans (including fueling stations)to assist student-athletes in achieving their dietary goals / objectives; Collaboration with sports medicine staff in medical nutrition therapy to assist with the management / treatment of medical conditions / diseases (sport and non-sport related); Collaboration with sports performance and sports medicine staffs in the assessment and analytics related to body composition as a tool to track progress and re-evaluate nutrition interventions; Collaboration with the sports medicine team in the education and in-patient / out-patient programming for medical and psychological conditions related to body image and eating disorders; Oversight of meal card program and reporting of meal frequency and attendance of student-athletes related to their nutritional needs; Relationship management with food providers and related vendors, ensuring that student-athletes are getting adequate nutritional ingredients / products (food, fluid, supplements) maximizing health and wellness, to include the development of a menu labeling system providing a complete nutritional analysis of each food item served; and Oversight of the sports nutrition budget, including procurement and payment for all nutritional supplements, student support, and the stocking/inventory/organization/cleaning of fueling stations. Due to the constituents it serves, position often requires work on evenings and weekends, in addition to potential occasional travel (team travel) as needed. Position requires a Master's degree in Nutrition/Dietetics, Food Sciences, Registered Dietitian or a closely related field and two (2) years of related experience or in the alternative, employer will accept a bachelor's degree Nutrition/Dietetics, Food Sciences, Registered Dietitian or closely related field and four (4) years of related experience. Accreditation as a Registered Dietitian (RD) through the Commission on Dietetic Registration and license/certification eligible in the State of Florida (ANSI-Conference for Food Protection) is required. Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time and occasional travel. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
    },
    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Coordinator--Facilities--Events-and-Operations_R114047": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Facilities, Events and Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics - Event Operations   The Coordinator for Facilities, Events, and Operations supports the daily management and execution of facility operations and athletic events for 16 Division I sports programs. This role works closely with internal staff and external partners to ensure efficient event coordination, facility upkeep, and operational excellence.   Key Responsibilities: Coordinate scheduling, setup, and breakdown for internal and external events  Serve as a liaison with third-party vendors and service providers  Manage gameday operations and event execution for assigned sports  Oversee parking operations for all football home games  Develop and manage staff onboarding processes and facility access control systems  Assist in planning and coordinating facility-related projects  Conduct weekly facility walkthroughs using standardized checklists  Monitor and manage FMX work orders to ensure timely completion  Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in a related field  At least one (1) year of relevant professional experience  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in facilities, events, or operations within intercollegiate athletics  Strong organizational, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills  Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment  Demonstrated commitment to integrity, professionalism, and compliance with NCAA, conference, and institutional regulations Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time and occasional travel. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
