    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Associate-Director---Brand-Design_R113265": {
      "title": "Associate Director, #Brand Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics - #Content   The Associate Director, #Brand Design, is a key member of the UCF Athletics Design Team. This role serves as the primary designer for both external football communications and football recruiting, while assisting with projects from the general Athletics Department on a limited basis. The Associate Director, #Brand Design is a talented, multi-disciplinary and collaborative designer, ready to position the UCF Athletics brand at the forefront of college athletics. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Collaborate with the Design team in the development, maintenance and advancement of the athletic department's brand identity through original and creative design concepts. Assist with the identification of opportunities to enhance brand identity where appropriate. Lead the development and execution of the UCF Football visual brand, with guidance from the Creative Director. Stay informed of current design trends and best practices, to produce efficient high-quality results. Create original designs for a variety of media, including both print and web design.  Includes, but is not limited to content for social media / new media platforms (website, email, advertising, etc.), as well as printed materials (posters, stationery, signage, large-scale facility graphics, etc.) Collaborate with external team (Social Media #Content, Football Recruiting, Brand Experience, Strategic Communications, ChargeOn Fund, Corporate Partnerships, Tickets, and Video #Content) in generating greater awareness of the UCF Football and Athletics brand, enhancing interest and attendance while maximizing overall revenue opportunities. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and two (2) years appropriate experience. Appropriate graduate coursework or master’s degree may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. A graphic design portfolio is required for consideration. Preferred Qualifications: Must show strong proficiency in Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator and InDesign. Collaborative mindset, openness to creative feedback, attention to detail, and strong communication skills (written/verbal) also necessary. Must be able to work autonomously, managing multiple project timelines and communication with various stakeholders, delivering completed projects within time sensitive deadlines. Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time and occasional travel. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
