    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Gameday-Staff---50-50-Sales_R113887": {
      "title": "Gameday Staff - 50/50 Sales",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics - Ticket Sales and Operations   Under the direction of a progressive ticket sales and operations unit, this position assists in the generation of revenue through the sale of 50/50 raffle tickets at home football games (and select other games). Responsibilities include, but not limited to: Facilitate and process \"50/50\" raffle ticket sales via electronic devices at stationary and / or mobile locations at scheduled UCF Athletics home games / events Proactively approach, engage, and invite fans to participate in Athletics' \"50/50\" raffle at each game / event, to include education of raffle details / rules and selling of tickets Accurately handle transactions from raffle ticket sales. Serve as a brand ambassador, representing UCF Athletics in a positive manner as brand ambassadors, while providing exceptional service to fans. Minimum qualifications: High School diploma Preferred qualifications: Previous experience in sales or speaking with groups.  Demonstrated interest in public speaking, networking and sales, as well as organizational / attention to detail and interpersonal skills also preferred.  Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position requires attendance at all scheduled home games / matches, which may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for \"world class\"  customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program.  Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
    },
    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Assistant-Director--Business---Finance_R113453": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Business & Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics - Business and Finance   Entry level position which assists with the operation of the Athletics Business Office (ABO) within UCF, Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations, serving as an ABO cost center liaison to process expenses and tasks as assigned. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Partner with assigned sports and administrative units in the processing and monitoring of expenses. Prepare and review budget reports and ledger accounts to identify miscoded items and suggest appropriate accounting adjustments. Ensure compliance with ABO policies and procedures related to all purchasing and travel related items for assigned cost centers. Reconcile expense card transactions accurately and timely for assigned cost centers. Process, track, and reconcile invoices and reimbursements within Workday for assigned cost centers. Review transactions and expense reports within Workday for completeness and accuracy for assigned cost centers. Monitor spend authorizations for repayment, reconciliation, and adherence to ABO policies and procedures. Assist with and complete month-end tasks, as well as year-end tasks and reporting related to cost centers. Provide training of Workday system and ABO policies and procedures to assigned units. Serve as a liaison with University Finance & Accounting related to assigned units. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and two (2) years appropriate experience. Appropriate graduate coursework or master’s degree may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business/finance or related field. Experience working in an athletics department. Experience using the Workday ERP. Proficient in Microsoft Office. Ability to think analytically and excitement to learn. Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time and occasional travel. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
    },
    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Game-Day-Staff-Assistant--Knights-Hospitality_R113224": {
      "title": "Game Day Staff Assistant, Knights Hospitality",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics - Knights Hospitality   UCF Athletics at the University of Central Florida, an NCAA Division I institution and Big 12 member, is seeking applications for Knights Hospitality staff (part time/events). As an integral member of the ChargeOn Fund team on UCF home game days and for affiliated special events, Knights Hospitality staff provide customer service and logistical support in the premium seating sections on football gamedays at Acrisure Bounce House, men’s basketball gamedays at Addition Financial Arena, and baseball gamedays John Euliano Park. Ideal candidates are individuals who embody energy, positivity, teamwork, and a proactive commitment to craft unforgettable moments for our premium season ticket members, donors, shareholders and visiting team and premium single game ticket buyers. 2026 Football Schedule (Home): UCF vs Bethune-Cookman: Thursday, September 3, 2026 (time TBD) | Opening Knight UCF vs Georgia State: Saturday, September 19, 2026 (time TBD) | Family Weekend UCF vs TCU: Saturday, September 26, 2026 (time TBD) UCF vs BYU: Saturday, October 24, 2026 (time TBD) Homecoming UCF vs Baylor: Friday, October 30, 2026 (time TBD) | Space Game UCF vs Arizona State: Saturday, November 14, 2026 (time TBD) | UCF vs Iowa State: Friday, November 20, 2026 (time TBD) | Senior Knight Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Providing exemplary customer service as liaisons between guests, catering staff, maintenance staff, custodial staff, and Athletics personnel.  Individual tasks may vary, but service will be a mix of event host, customer service, donor relations, greeting/ushering, wristbanding, maintaining integrity of premium area, etc.  As such, selected candidates are expected to be actively engaged in all home football games (game times TBD).   Please note that Knights Hospitality staff who show exemplary effort during football season will be offered the opportunity to work UCF men’s basketball and baseball games, as well as additional affiliate events, as appropriate. Past opportunities have included supporting high-profile events such as the NFL Pro Bowl Skills Challenge and Bowl Games, offering staff the chance to gain valuable experience at nationally recognized sporting events beyond campus. With the opening of the new Roth Tower, there will also be opportunity to support corporate/special events. Minimum Qualifications: Must be at least 18 years old Professional resume required Preferred Qualifications: Prefer previous customer service experience. Strong attention to detail, teamwork and communication (written/verbal) skills. Proactivity in high pressure situations is also preferred.  Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time and occasional travel. As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for customer service and knowing / complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
    },
    "https://ucf.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Orlando-FL-Main-Campus/Game-Day-Staff-Assistant--Athletics-Production_R111752-1": {
      "title": "Game Day Staff Assistant, Athletics Production",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-09-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: UCF Athletics - Production   Under the oversight of the Senior Associate A.D./Executive Producer of Athletics Production, the staff assistant will support game day production for in-venue and streaming platforms. Multiple individuals will be selected for the team as appropriate. Selected candidates are expected to be actively engaged home games across multiple sports for UCF Athletics, with assignments frequently scheduled on nights and weekends.   Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Production engineering Technical director Audio & video Camera operations, including replay Announcers Utilities   Minimum Qualifications: Must be at least 18 years old   Preferred Qualifications: Work hard Strong attention to detail Communication Team Player Be passionate   Due to the nature/scope of Athletics and Athletics events, position may require work during evenings, weekends, and holidays, as well as the ability to stand / walk for extended periods of time.   As a staff member of UCF Athletics, the selected candidate will be a person of integrity and character who shares a commitment for knowing and complying with NCAA, Conference, and institutional rules as they apply to the UCF Athletics program. Salary: Negotiable Please note that UCF Athletics operates as a Direct Support Organization (DSO) of the University of Central Florida, with different payroll and benefits than university employees. If interested in positions with the university, please click Here to visit their website. As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, our mission is to positively transform the lives of our students academically, athletically and personally through a nationally competitive intercollegiate athletics program that enhances the reputation and visibility of the university. We strive to be Florida's preeminent athletic program representing UCF and our community with distinction on the national stage as “Orlando's Hometown Team.”   UCF Athletics values our employees and working for us has its perks, including:   Benefit packages: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurances, Flexible Spending & Health Savings Accounts, and Employee Assistance Program Wellness initiatives: UCF Athletics is recognized by Cigna Healthcare with the silver level Healthy Workforce Designation for our commitment to employee well-being and vitality through our benefits offerings, wellness platform and programming Paid time off for applicable positions, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays   Retirement savings options    Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions    Tickets to UCF sporting events Education assistance    To learn more about UCF and the Knights, visit our websites at ucf.edu and ucfknights.com ."
